# Cinematic Polish Skill

Use this skill when the user asks to apply Hollywood-grade polish — color grading, film grain, vignette, or audio mixing.

## The single highest-ROI move

`mattdesl/glsl-lut` + IWLTBAP Blade Runner 2049 LUT + HolyGrain 35mm grain + CSS radial vignette. ~80 LOC. ~4 hours. Audience reaction shifts from "nice website" to "is this a movie?" Build this Day 2 before anything else.

## Required asset downloads (do this first)

1. **LUT file:** Download from [luts.iwltbap.com](https://luts.iwltbap.com) — pick "Blade Runner 2049" pack. Need the `.cube` file. Convert to `.png` LUT image (HALD format, 33×33×33 unwrapped to 1089×33 PNG) using [LUT Converter](https://github.com/mattdesl/lut-converter) or via a `.cube → .png` online tool.
2. **Film grain:** Download from [holygrain.com/free-film-grain-download](https://www.holygrain.com/free-film-grain-download/). Pick "35mm Grain Pack". Drop the .mov file into `/public/grain/35mm-overlay.webm` (transcode to WebM via FFmpeg: `ffmpeg -i 35mm.mov -c:v libvpx-vp9 -b:v 2M 35mm-overlay.webm`).
3. **Audio bed:** Subscribe to [Musicbed](https://www.musicbed.com). Pull 3 tracks from Tony Anderson, Christoffer Moe Ditlevsen, Gavin Luke, or Hill. Save as `/public/audio/bed-anticipation.mp3`, `bed-build.mp3`, `bed-resolution.mp3`.

## The implementation

### Step 1: Color-graded video backdrop

```tsx
// src/components/chrome/ColorGradedVideo.tsx
"use client";
import { useEffect, useRef } from "react";
import createLUT from "glsl-lut";
import REGL from "regl";

export function ColorGradedVideo({ src }: { src: string }) {
  const canvasRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement>(null);
  const videoRef = useRef<HTMLVideoElement>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!canvasRef.current || !videoRef.current) return;
    const regl = REGL({ canvas: canvasRef.current });
    
    const lutTexture = regl.texture({ src: "/luts/blade-runner-2049.png" });
    const videoTexture = regl.texture(videoRef.current);
    
    const drawLUT = createLUT({
      regl,
      texture: videoTexture,
      lut: lutTexture,
    });

    const tick = () => {
      videoTexture.subimage(videoRef.current!);
      drawLUT();
      requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    };
    tick();
  }, [src]);

  return (
    <>
      <video 
        ref={videoRef} 
        src={src} 
        autoPlay muted loop playsInline 
        className="hidden"
      />
      <canvas ref={canvasRef} className="fixed inset-0 w-screen h-screen object-cover" />
    </>
  );
}
```

### Step 2: Film grain + vignette overlays

```tsx
// src/components/chrome/CinematicOverlays.tsx
export function CinematicOverlays() {
  return (
    <>
      {/* Film grain — actual 35mm scan, not CSS noise */}
      <video
        src="/grain/35mm-overlay.webm"
        autoPlay muted loop playsInline
        className="fixed inset-0 w-screen h-screen pointer-events-none"
        style={{ mixBlendMode: "overlay", opacity: 0.15 }}
      />
      
      {/* Radial vignette — pure CSS, 6 lines */}
      <div
        className="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none"
        style={{
          background: "radial-gradient(ellipse at center, transparent 40%, rgba(0,0,0,0.6) 100%)",
          mixBlendMode: "multiply",
        }}
      />
    </>
  );
}
```

