## The audio mix (3-layer architecture)

```ts
// src/lib/audio.ts
import { Howl } from "howler";

// LAYER 1: Hero ambient bed (always playing, -22dB)
export const ambientBed = new Howl({
  src: ["/audio/bed-anticipation.mp3"],
  loop: true,
  volume: 0.12, // -22dB
});

// LAYER 2: Act-specific swells (-15dB at peaks)
export const stinger = new Howl({
  src: ["/audio/stinger-wing-transition.mp3"], // 1.5s Udio-generated
  volume: 0.32, // -10dB
});

// LAYER 3: Howler SFX sprite
export const sfx = new Howl({
  src: ["/audio/ui-sprite.mp3"],
  sprite: {
    press:    [0,    300],
    confirm:  [400,  500],
    hover:    [1000, 200],
    whoosh:   [1300, 1200],
    comms:    [2600, 800],
    boot:     [3500, 3000],
    error:    [6600, 400],
    hum:      [7100, 12000, true], // looping
  },
  volume: 0.4, // -8dB
});

// Audio leads visual by 60ms — call this BEFORE the visual change
export function playSfx(sound: keyof typeof sfx._sprite) {
  sfx.play(sound);
  return new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 60));
}
```

## The Mission Impossible countdown (45-second video gen filler)

When the Video Generator sub-tool runs, fill the 45-second wait with cinematic tension:

```tsx
// src/components/tools/cmo/VideoCountdown.tsx
import { motion } from "motion/react";
import { DecryptedText } from "@/components/chrome/DecryptedText"; // from shadcn.io

const statusMessages = [
  "INITIALIZING DIFFUSION MODEL...",
  "FRAMES ANALYZED: 247 / 720",
  "COMPOSITING PASS 3 OF 7",
  "RENDERING SHOT 02...",
  "COLOR GRADING APPLIED",
  "FINAL OUTPUT: 89%",
];

export function VideoCountdown({ onComplete }: { onComplete: () => void }) {
  return (
    <div className="fixed inset-0 flex items-center justify-center">
      {/* Layer 1: Decrypt status text (cycles every 4s) */}
      <DecryptedText text={statusMessages} interval={4000} />

      {/* Layer 2: Radial countdown ring */}
      <motion.svg className="w-96 h-96">
        <motion.circle
          cx="50%" cy="50%" r="45%"
          stroke="#00d4ff" strokeWidth="4" fill="none"
          initial={{ pathLength: 1 }}
          animate={{ pathLength: 0 }}
          transition={{ duration: 45, ease: "linear" }}
          style={{ filter: "drop-shadow(0 0 20px #00d4ff)" }}
        />
      </motion.svg>

      {/* Layer 3: Audio waveform visualizer (Tone.js analyzer of ambientBed) */}
      <WaveformCanvas />
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Acceptance criteria (Day 2 deliverable)
- [ ] One Seedance backdrop clip displayed through `ColorGradedVideo`
- [ ] Film grain overlay visible at 15% opacity
- [ ] Radial vignette darkens corners
- [ ] Ambient bed plays at -22dB (audible but never dominant)
- [ ] SFX sprite tested — press, confirm, comms-ping all working
- [ ] Audio leads visual by 60ms on press handlers

If all 6 pass, walk into another room, look at the screen from 25 feet — does it look like a website or a movie? That's the test.

## The Hollywood checklist (run before every act)

Before any beat ships, walk through these 9 questions. If any answer is no, fix it.

1. Is there a film reference for every visible element?
2. Is the ambient bed playing under everything?
3. Is there a single focal point per moment, or am I splitting attention?
4. Does typography read from the back row of the venue (body 64pt+)?
5. Are colors graded (cyan/amber/void only)?
6. Does the SFX lead the visual by 60ms?
7. Does the entrance animation use expo-out, not linear?
8. Is ≥40% of the screen empty (negative space rule)?
9. Would Perception Studio ship this for Iron Man Mark VII?
